      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Unlimited public avatar favorites and global avatar search were the only reason I paid for VRC+ subscriptions to enable such features from emmVRC.\nI like all those beautiful and unique avatars and worlds I have encountered and would like to revisit them again. I cherish those amazing things created by the community.\nAuthors who dislike their avatars being favorited have always been able to set them to private and be unavailable for the public to clone. \nAuthors who wanted their creations to be shared shall be shared instead of removed due to limited favorite slots or long forgotten in some avatar worlds. \nEmmVRC has always been working like this. If the Devs take such a feature away, they better implement it back in for at least the subscribers.\nI wish to say the same for favoriting worlds, but that’s another topic.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-05-18T13:08:30.061Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "VRC+ was positioned as \"nice-to-have extras for people who chose to support the game\", and I'd like to argue that current avatar favorites paywalling approach goes against that.\nFor people who use mostly public avatars, a single group limited to 25 favorites is extremely limiting. For many, even four groups with 25 slots each would still be not enough. As evidenced by many users of *carefully kept text files with avatar IDs*, having over four groups, over 100 favorites, or over 25 favorites in a group is not uncommon. Not every favorited avatar is used daily, but the ability to quickly pull out that one specific meme avatar (after easily finding it in the appropriate group labelled \"memes\") is invaluable in some social situations.\nFor prolific avatar creators, the deal is especially bad. They bring value to the platform by creating content for it, and all they get in return is a single laggy list with everything they have ever made that is impossible to find something specific in. At least that one is unlimited. And sorting out this mess requires sacrificing severely limited avatar favorite slots/groups that could have been used for cool public avatars they stumble upon.\nLast, but not least, there are tons of ways to go around those limits - uploading worlds with pedestals, using Udon or editor scripts to automate pedestal creation from *carefully kept text files with avatar IDs*, using standalone API-interacting apps to change contents of (limited) favorite groups, and probably more ways I haven't considered. Most of them range from mildly inconvenient to highly inconvenient.\nAs it stands right now, the limits, and the paywall, are set out not to \"give a nice extra\", but to punish and/or inconvenience the most active and/or valuable users of the platform - it's pretty much \"pay or suffer, and if you're very active suffer even if you pay\", not \"thanks for your support\". You don't want to be seen as a greedy evil corp, do you?\nHow would I suggest changing the system?\n* First, let everyone create, rename, and remove avatar favorite groups as they see fit, and remove size limit on a group. Total group count can be limited, but the limit has to be high enough that people who make moderately sized groups (say 10+ favorites) will hit total favorites limit before group limit.\nThis might require UI rework, as the current UI is ill-suited to this.\n* Second, rebalance total favorite limit so that VRC+ upgrade is \"a nice extra\" indeed - for example, have the baseline limit at 100 (which is much more likely to cover the needs of most active players than measly 25), and have VRC+ provide either unlimited favorites (your upcoming competitors already do that without a paywall, by the way), or some very high number that would be impractical to use if reached, like 1000.\nIn an ideal world, avatar favorites would not be a VRC+ feature (social/world favorites aren't, after all), and everyone would get treated equally well with an impractical-to-reach high limit like a thousand (or unlimited). Not to mention that *carefully kept text files* are technically unlimited too, if inconvenient.\n* Additionally, to alleviate creators' pains with sorting own avatars, make favorited own avatars not count against favorites limit (the \"uploaded by me\" icon will be useful for something for once).\n* Improve general list UI/UX - having more groups/lists would require a better approach to reduce scrolling, such as being able to fully collapse a list to just its header, persist collapse/expansion state across menu reopens and game restarts, completely hide lists the user doesn't want to see (ahem default avatars), and so on. This point probably requires its own post in feature requests?\nSome of these points can be easily applied to social and world favorites too - more slots and more control over grouping would be a welcome change.",
